14. Reimbursement of expenses.– (1) If a landlord fails to pay a tax, fee or charge relating to the premises, the concerned authority may direct the tenant to pay the tax, fee or charge.
(2) The tenant shall pay the tax, fee or charge relating to the premises and defray the amount from the rent or file an application against the landlord in the Rent Tribunal for the recovery of the amount of tax, fee or charge paid by him.
